Surely goodness and mercy shall follow me all the days of my life;
an I will dwell in the house of the Lord forever.

Jesus on me bestow,
The penitent desire;
With true sincerity of wo
My aching breast inspire;

I lay my body down to sleep;
Peace is the pillow for my head;
His ever-watchful eye will keep
Its constant guard around my bed.

Good news, good news to Ad­am’s race;

Let Christ­ians all agree,

To sing re­deem­ing love and grace;

This is the Ju­bi­lee.

Sinners, be wise, re­turn and come

Unto the Sav­ior free;

The Spir­it bids you wel­come on;

This is the Ju­bi­lee.

O all who dwell in for­eign lands,

In want and pov­er­ty;

Return and come to Ca­naan’s land;

This is the Ju­bi­lee.

Let persecution rage around,
And antichrist appear,
My silent dust beneath the ground,
There’s no disturbance there.
Though I can never come to thee;
Let not this grieve your heart;
For you will shortly come to me,
Where we shall never part.
